.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH terminal-of-tinsel-quiz 1  "quiz " 
.SH NAME
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-quiz \- Pull a cracker: the Christmas Cracker Quiz
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBterminal\-of\-tinsel quiz\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-questions\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-pack\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fINAME\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Multiple\-choice questions built from the creature data: facts, quotes, first appearances, film credits and myth checks. Every answer explains itself. Name a creature to be quizzed only about that one.
.PP
With \-\-json the questions are printed with their answers instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the command\*(Aqs data as JSON instead of drawing it (errors become a JSON object on stderr)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-questions\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 10]
Number of questions
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Plain output: no colour, no emoji, ASCII borders (also set by NO_COLOR, or by piping)
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR \fI<PACK>\fR
Only use creatures from these packs, e.g. \-\-pack nordic,dickens
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
Only ask about this creature
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  terminal\-of\-tinsel quiz
  terminal\-of\-tinsel quiz \-n 5
  terminal\-of\-tinsel quiz yule cat
  terminal\-of\-tinsel quiz \-\-pack nordic
